OL,5,G1800 Choral Evensong
OL,6,     FFrom the Chapel of The Queen's
OL,7,     FCollege, Oxford, with music by
OL,8,     FDarke, Howells and Bach.
OL,9,G1900 Sunday Feature: A Musical Evening
OL,10,G     at Monticello
OL,11,     FMichael Goldfarb takes a look at
OL,12,     Fthe role music played in Thomas
OL,13,     FJefferson's life.
OL,14,G1945 Words and Music
OL,15,     FIt's summer holiday time so we're
OL,16,     Fheading to the beach for seaside
OL,17,     Fprose and poetry from Marcel
OL,18,     FProust to Enid Blyton and music
OL,19,     Ffrom Mendelssohn to The Beach
OL,20,     FBoys.
